    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 185\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5637-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to create a temporary commission relating to the office of\n      mental health housing programs\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would create  an  Office  of  Mental  Health  (OMH)  Housing\nProgram  Evaluation  Commission (\"the Commission\"). The Commission would\nmake recommendations as to the number of sites and of quarterly occupan-\ncy levels for scattered  site  supportive  housing,  licensed  community\nresidences,  licensed treatment apartments, and other supportive housing\n(housing programs). Members of the Commission would be appointed by  the\nGovernor  and the Legislature and be required to issue a report on hous-\ning, residences, and apartments no later than October 1, 2020, including\nany recommendations for legislative action.\n \n  While the needs of housing for clients served  by  OMH  are  certainly\ngreat,  this  measure is wholly redundant to the work that OMH currently\nperforms. Since the 1990s, OMH has transformed residential treatment for\nindividuals with serious mental illnesses from institutional to communi-\nty settings. New York State currently leads the nation in the amount  of\nfunded  housing units compared to any other state. Furthermore, the 2020\nFY Enacted Budget included an additional $10 million to enhance  funding\nfor existing supportive housing and single residency programs, the fifth\nyear in a row that support for these programs was included in the Execu-\ntive Budget, bringing the total to over $50 million on an annual basis.\n \n  The  functions outlined in this legislation are already carried out by\nOMH as part of its core mission. This Commission would rely  on  OMH  to\nprovide  assistance  in  the  form of staffing, technical assistance and\nother resources to accomplish their legislatively defined tasks.  Howev-\ner, the Legislature has not identified  a  source  of  funding  for  the\nCommission  or  the significant costs to implement. Lastly, although the\nlegislation refers to the Commission as \"temporary,\" there is no  sunset\ndate in the legislation. For these reasons, I am constrained to veto the\nbill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
